<gretldata version="1.3" name="canada5" frequency="4" startobs="1990:1" endobs="2014:4" type="time-series">
<description> canada5.def (time series data)

      dateid01 gap fngap inf infex t

	Obs:  100 quarterly observations from 1990Q1 to 2014Q4

	dateid01 01 month year
	gap	 Output gap for Canada: deviation of GDP from HP-filtered GDP in percentage of HP-filtered GDP.
	fngap	 Finance neutral output gap for Canada. The HP filter is augmented with financial cycle information.
	inf	 Inflation rate for Canada, percent. Year-over-year change in the CPI.
	infex	 Inflationary expectations for Canada. A survey measure for the coming 4 quarters.
	t	 A time trend, t=1 for 1990Q1, t=2 for 1990Q2, ...

Note: HP refers to the Hodrick-Prescott filter (Journal of Money, Credit and Banking 29 (1997), p.1-16.)

Data source: The data were kindly provided by Johanna Amberger from their study: Amberger, J., R Fendel and H. Stremmel (2017), ?Improved output gaps with financial cycle information? An application to G7 countries? new Keynesian Phillips curves?, Applied Economics Letters, 24(4), 219-228. 

More details about the construction of the variables can be found in the Applied Economics Letters paper.



